The keystroke was never the slow part. The list update pretending to be as urgent as the keystroke was. Once React knows the difference, it stops making you choose between "fast typing" and "correct results" — you get both: the keystroke in one render, the list in the next.

Where else in your app is one setState secretly doing two jobs at two different urgencies? I'd bet you can name one from memory.




